V2.1.3 — PHASE A CORRECTNESS FREEZE (audit response)
=================================================================

Triggered by the post-V2.1.2 audit identifying 5 code-level issues:
  2.1 vol-targeting uses forward returns (timing look-ahead)
  2.2 OOS slices restart vol history (20-bar zero warmup per fold)
  2.5 discovery discards hold_bars/threshold when evaluating OOS
  2.4 drawdown control applied today's return for today's weight
  2.7/2.15 trial counter == n_trials_global (both cumulative); no per-run delta

Fixes applied:
  - backtest() gains explicit risk_returns param (observable trailing
    close-to-close). scale[t] now uses only information known at close[t-1].
  - backtest() accepts a context frame for warm-start vol state.
  - Discovery pins per-fold thresholds + hold_bars and replays them via the
    fixed_thresholds mechanism (no discard).
  - Drawdown control state shifted to t-1 (causal).
  - run.py captures start_count; records trials_this_experiment (per-run
    delta) alongside n_trials_global (cumulative high-water).
  - Version bumped to V2.1.3; fresh artifacts_real_v4 run.

